<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="TheSheikofAraby-Bb-Theme" spTempo="200">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1921
Composer:	Ted Snyder
Lyricist:	Harry B. Smith and Francis Wheeler
Form:	ABAC (verse and chorus)
Style:	Early jazz / Tin Pan Alley; commonly played in a swing or Dixieland style
Key:	B-flat major (commonly cited original key)

Written as a Tin Pan Alley song amid the popularity of the
Rudolph Valentino film The Sheik, it became a hit and was
later adopted by early jazz bands, particularly in
New Orleans. Jazz arrangements commonly feature the
chorus; the original song also has a verse that leads into it.</spComments>
